Wolfi deviation (docs/deviations.md, "orchestrator entrypoint.sh shebang"): the script starts with #!/bin/sh
but uses bash syntax: `$(</var/run/secrets/.../namespace)` and `$(<$PATH_TO_SECRET/$TOPOLOGY_USER)` (the
Kubernetes namespace and the topology password). On UBI 9 /bin/sh is bash; on Wolfi it is busybox ash, where
`$(<file)` expands to an empty string, so the namespace and the password would be lost. Run it with bash.

--- a/entrypoint.sh
+++ b/entrypoint.sh
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-#!/bin/sh
+#!/bin/bash
 set -e

 export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/orchestrator
